---
// The one moving figure on the site: oscillation against advance, after Robert Fritz.
// CSS only. Under reduced motion both markers rest in a meaningful position.
---

<div class="tracks" role="img" aria-label="Two tracks. On the first, a marker swings back and forth between problem and relief. On the second, a marker moves steadily from what is to what is wanted.">
  <div class="track osc" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="lane"><span class="tick a"></span><span class="tick b"></span><span class="mover"></span></div>
    <p class="caps"><span class="at-a">Problem</span><span class="at-b">Relief</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="track adv" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="lane"><span class="trail"></span><span class="tick a"></span><span class="tick b"></span><span class="mover"></span></div>
    <p class="caps"><span>What is</span><span>What is wanted</span></p>
  </div>
</div>
